course: dictionary
lesson: 901
title: Bitter: one word, many meanings
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Bitter has more than one meaning, so use the context to choose the right one. «Lick a lemon and it is sour; taste a tiny pinch of baking soda and it is bitter and soapy.» The words taste and soapy tell you bitter is about a strong, sharp, unpleasant taste.
explain: «It was bitter cold on the hill.» Here bitter means extremely cold. Check it by swapping in very cold: the sentence still makes sense. Now try «The bitter wind howled.» The wind is not a taste, so bitter means cold again.
explain: Bitter can also describe feelings. Bitter feelings are angry and hurt because something unfair happened. «They fought to the bitter end» means until the very end, even when it is hard. Always ask: which meaning fits this sentence?
fact: Bitter is an adjective, so it describes a noun, such as a bitter taste or a bitter wind.
fact: Bitter has five meanings: a sharp, unpleasant taste; extremely cold; angry, hurt feelings; a very hard fight; and, in the UK, a kind of beer.
fact: Bitter is one of the five tastes the tongue can sense: sweet, sour, salty, bitter and umami.
fact: Many poisons and unsafe plants taste bitter, so a bitter taste can be a warning to stop and not eat.
fact: «To the bitter end» means until the very end, even if it is hard.
exercise: «Taste a tiny pinch of baking soda and it is bitter and soapy.» What does bitter mean here? | *A strong, sharp, unpleasant taste | A kind of beer | Extremely cold | Angry and hurt
exercise: Why do makers add sweet flavours to medicines for children? | Because medicines are always sour | Because children do not like sweet things | Because sweet flavours make medicines colder | *Because many medicines are naturally bitter
exercise: «It was bitter cold on the hill.» What does bitter mean in this sentence? | Sour and sharp | Angry | *Extremely cold | Sweet and sticky
test: «The bitter feelings lasted for years after the unfair game.» What does bitter mean here? | Extremely cold | A kind of beer | *Angry and hurt because something unfair happened | A strong, sharp taste
test: «They fought to the bitter end.» What does to the bitter end mean? | Without any fighting at all | Until lunchtime | *Until the very end, even if it is hard | Only for a short time
exam: Ben says bitter always means cold. Is he right? | No, bitter always means sweet | *No, bitter can mean a taste, cold weather, angry feelings, a hard fight or a beer | Yes, but only when someone is angry | Yes, bitter always means cold
